// Code the program did not write.
//
// A function every clause of which another module's macro wrote (an
// Elixir `use`), or that an OTP header or a parser generator defined
// (Erlang: yecc's runtime from yeccpre.hrl, an installed application's
// include), is `macro_written` (Argus.Extractors.Generated). It is a
// library's when its writer is none of the program's modules: its call
// sites and handlers are the library's protocol, and a finding would
// point at a `use` line or a generated parser, where the program has
// nothing to change. A `use` of the program's own macro is the program's
// code, and is judged as such.
//
// Requires imports.dl and an analysis that runs the Generated extractor.

.decl library_written(func: symbol)

library_written(f) :-
  macro_written(f),
  macro_generated(f, by),
  !program_module(by).

.decl program_module(mod: symbol)

program_module(m) :- function_def(_, m, _, _, _).
